[[File:S2E49 Void 2.png|thumb|170px|[[Void]], the Nullifier scout]]
According to legend, the Nullifers were a group of unimaginably evil beings that originated from [[Huntik]]. {{source|Chasing Void}} Long before recorded history, a single Nullifier scout, [[Void]], found Earth by chance and created the [[Spiral Mark]] as a beacon to signal his brethren to Earth. {{source|Words from Eathon}} They were opposed by [[Lord Casterwill]], the first [[Seeker]], who summoned the [[Titans]] to Earth to fight a war against this threat. After a fierce 500-year conflict, Lord Casterwill was finally able to defeat the Nullifiers, and sealed the [[Spiral Mark]] with a powerful spell so that no evil Seekers could ever gain use of it. This spell could only be broken by the [[Willblade]] and the power of [[Void]] on the longest night of the year with the [[Red Comet]] approaching Earth. {{source|The Spiral Mark}} 

After the death of Lord Casterwill, however, his [[the Betrayer|most trusted friend]] betrayed Casterwill and his [[Casterwill family|family]], by attempting to call the Nullifiers back to Earth by performing a dark ritual at the Spiral Mark. In his hand was the [[Amulet]] of Void. {{Source|Chasing Void}} The Betrayer had enchanted a Nullifier artifact, the [[Necklace of Tutankhamun]], to control the Nullifiers. {{Source|Rassimov's Secret}} This time, the Betrayer was opposed by the [[Elder son of Casterwill|elder]] and [[Younger son of Casterwill|younger]] sons and the [[Elder daughter of Casterwill|elder]] and [[Younger daughter of Casterwill|younger]] daughters of Casterwill, as well as his [[Champion of Casterwill|Champion]]. After another conflict, they defeated the Betrayer and sealed the Mark again, preventing the return of the Nullifiers. {{source|Chasing Void}}

Void's Amulet was taken into safekeeping by the [[Casterwill family]] where it remained for generations until, in the modern age, [[the Organization]] managed to steal it from them. It was then kept in [[Klaus' bookshop]]. {{Source|Chasing Void}} Eventually, despite the attempts of the [[Huntik Foundation]] to recover it, the Amulet fell into the hands of [[Blood Spiral]], a group devoted to bringing back the Nullifiers to end all civilization. {{Source|The Blood Spiral}} 

[[File:S2E49 Rassimov summons Void hunters.png|thumb|170px|Rassimov summons Void]]

On the longest night of the year, Rassimov summoned [[Void]] to reveal the [[Spiral Mark]] once more. {{source|Words from Eathon}}  Following the revelation that the [[Red Comet]] had changed course to hit the spot of the Spiral Mark, Rassimov revealed his own scheme to double cross the Betrayer and the other Spirals, planning to control the Nullifiers with the [[Necklace of Tutankhamun]]. Void teleported Rassimov into space to the Red Comet. However, as the Comet collided with the pair, the Necklace was disintegrated and Rassimov was killed in the process, although the status of Void remains unknown. {{Source|The Spiral Mark}}

The Betrayer had set events into motion to allow for his own return. Using his own power, the Betrayer was able to activate the Spiral Mark and  for the return of the Nullifiers before he was defeated by the [[Casterwill family|Casterwill]]-[[Huntik Foundation|Foundation]] alliance. However, despite the defeat of the Betrayer, the Spiral Mark still appeared to be active, and could be seen flickering far across the galaxy.{{Source|Dante's Return}}

